 — Groq Whisper"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-ink-2 lg:col-span-7","children":"Speech-to-text on the input path, so asking costs a sentence instead of a window change and a paragraph of typing."}]]}],["$","li","Vision and reasoning — LLaMA 4 Scout",{"className":"grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2 py-6 lg:grid-cols-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-baseline gap-4 lg:col-span-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"num font-mono text-mono tracking-[0.13em] text-ink-4","children":"03"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-h4 font-medium text-ink","children":"Vision and reasoning — LLaMA 4 Scout"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-ink-2 lg:col-span-7","children":"A vision-capable model, so the companion can work from what’s actually on screen rather than from the user’s description of it. This is what makes the voice path viable: “what’s wrong with this?” is only a usable query if the model can see the “this.”"}]]}],["$","li","Application shell — Electron, React, TypeScript",{"className":"grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2 py-6 lg:grid-cols-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-baseline gap-4 lg:col-span-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"aria-hidden":"true","className":"num font-mono text-mono tracking-[0.13em] text-ink-4","children":"04"}],["$","h4",null,{"className":"text-h4 font-medium text-ink","children":"Application shell — Electron, React, TypeScript"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-ink-2 lg:col-span-7","children":"Electron for the OS-level window behaviour that a web app cannot do. React and TypeScript for the interface, with types carrying the contract between the audio pipeline, the vision context and the response surface."}]]}],["$","li","Instrumentation layer",{"className":"grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2 py-6 lg:grid-cols-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-baseline gap-4 lg:col-span-5","children":["$L2f","$L30"]}],"$L31"]}]]}]}],"$L32","$L33"]}]]}]
